The data mentioned above is processed for the following purposes only:
- Providing, operating and securing the Service (technical connection data);
- Remembering your display and language preferences to improve your comfort across sessions (localStorage);
- Letting you find your recent operation history directly on your device;
- Recording your consent (or lack thereof) regarding local storage that is not strictly necessary, as required by applicable regulation.

In accordance with Article 6 of the GDPR, each processing activity rests on an identified legal basis:
- Performance of the service requested by the user (art. 6.1.b) for local processing of your files and for storing the functional preferences essential to the Service;
- The publisher’s legitimate interest (art. 6.1.f) for technical security logs and abuse prevention;
- Your consent (art. 6.1.a), where required, for any local storage or cookie that is not strictly necessary for the Service to function — collected through the cookie management module.

Your data is never sold, rented, or shared for commercial purposes with third parties. The only possible recipients are:
- Our host, Vercel Inc., acting as a processor for the technical hosting of the Service;
- Competent administrative or judicial authorities, only where required by law.

In accordance with the GDPR and, where applicable, Cameroonian legislation on the protection of personal data, you have the following rights over data we actually hold about you (technical connection data):
- Right of access;
- Right of rectification of inaccurate data;
- Right to erasure ("right to be forgotten");
- Right to restriction of processing;
- Right to object on legitimate grounds;
- Right to data portability, where applicable;
- Right to lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority (e.g. your national data protection authority in the EU, or the competent Cameroonian authority for data protection).

For any data stored locally (theme, language, history), you exercise these rights yourself, directly and at any time, from the Service’s Settings page or your browser’s privacy settings, with no need to contact us. For any other request, write to [TO BE COMPLETED — dedicated contact email address, e.g. contact@yourdomain.com].

By using the Service, you agree to:
- Use the Service in accordance with its intended purpose and in compliance with applicable laws and regulations;
- Only process, through the Service, files for which you legally hold the rights or authorization of use (copyright, related rights, image rights, third-party personal data, confidentiality of correspondence, etc.);
- Not use the Service for unlawful or fraudulent purposes, or to produce, alter or distribute illegal content (counterfeiting, content falsified for fraud, content infringing third-party rights, etc.);
- Not attempt to disrupt, overload, bypass security measures of, or reverse-engineer the Service beyond what the law permits.

As of the date of this policy, ONE does not use:
- Any advertising cookie or tracker;
- Any third-party audience-analytics tool (such as Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, etc.);
- Any social-network cookie;
- Any data reseller or third-party ad broker.

Should this change, this policy will be updated beforehand and your consent will be requested where applicable.

You can, at any time:
- Change your choice via the "Manage cookies" link available in the Service’s footer;
- Clear your local history from the Service’s Settings page;
- Delete all local storage related to ONE from your browser’s privacy settings ("Clear browsing data" / "Cookies and site data");
- Configure your browser to block local storage by default, at the possible cost of losing your preferences between visits.

Should a paid offering (subscription, one-time purchase, or donation) be introduced in the future, the following principles would apply, subject to dedicated Terms of Sale published before that offering launches:
- For consumers residing in the European Union, a 14-calendar-day right of withdrawal would apply to purchases of digital content, unless you expressly request immediate performance and thereby waive your right of withdrawal once the digital service has been fully performed (Article L221-28 of the French Consumer Code, or the equivalent provision of your national law);
- For other users, refund terms would be specified in the Terms of Sale applicable at the time of purchase, in accordance with Cameroonian law and the law applicable at the buyer’s place of residence;
- Any refund would remain excluded in cases of abusive use of the Service, proven fraud, or where the digital service has been fully performed with the user’s prior, express agreement.
